      "text": "arXiv:math/0110009v3 [math.MG] 3 Sep 2003 — We develop an analogue for sphere packing of the linear programming bounds for error-correcting codes, and use it to prove upper bounds for the density of\n\n**arXiv:math/0110009v3 [math.MG] 3 Sep 2003**\n\n*By Henry Cohn and Noam Elkies**\n\n26 pp, 14 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We develop an analogue for sphere packing of the linear programming bounds for error-correcting codes, and use it to prove upper bounds for the density of sphere packings, which are the best bounds known at least for di- mensions 4 through 36. We conjecture that our approach can be used to solve the sphere packing problem in dimensions 8 and 24.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Abstract; Contents; 1 Introduction; 2 Lattices, Fourier transforms, and Poisson su; 3 Principal theorems; 4 Homogeneous spaces; 5 Conditions for a sharp bound; 6 Stationary points; 7 Numerical results; 8 Uniqueness; Appendix A Technicalities about density; Appendix B Other convex bodies; Appendix C Numerical data",
